    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Jeremy earns per room by the number of rooms he cleaned. Jeremy earns \\(\\dfrac{11}{2}\\) dollars per room and cleaned \\(\\dfrac{7}{3}\\) rooms. Therefore, we need to compute the product \\(\\dfrac{11}{2} \\times \\dfrac{7}{3}\\).\n\nThe multiplication of two fractions \\(\\dfrac{a}{b} \\times \\dfrac{c}{d}\\) is given by \\(\\dfrac{a \\times c}{b \\times d}\\). Applying this to our problem, we get:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{11}{2} \\times \\dfrac{7}{3} = \\dfrac{11 \\times 7}{2 \\times 3} = \\dfrac{77}{6}\n\\]\n\nThus, Steven owes Jeremy \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{77}{6}}\\) dollars.",
